$ so git --help
Bring history in from git, or send it back

Usage: so git [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  import  Bring a git repository's history in
  export  Send the store's history to a git repository

Examples (SWARMOPS_REPO names the store, SWARMOPS_AGENT you):
  $ git init --bare app.git
  $ so git export app.git --ref main --branch main
  $ so git import app.git --ref main --into from-git

Learn more:
  A command's help  so git <command> --help
  Guide             https://swarmops.cc/docs/guides/git-round-trip
  Reference         https://swarmops.cc/docs/reference/cli

Options:
      --repo <STORE>     The store to use (default: $SWARMOPS_REPO)
      --as <AGENT>       The agent to act as, <family>/<instance> (default:
                         $SWARMOPS_AGENT)
      --json             Print the JSON envelope: the default, unless
                         $SWARMOPS_FORMAT is human
      --human            Print a short text rendering instead of JSON
      --pretty[=<BOOL>]  Pretty-print the JSON (default: when stdout is a
                         terminal)
  -h, --help             Print help

$ so remote --help
Add, remove or list the store's git remotes

Usage: so remote [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Record a git remote in the store
  remove  Forget a git remote, and the mirror's refs of it
  list    List the store's git remotes

Examples (SWARMOPS_REPO names the store, SWARMOPS_AGENT you):
  $ so remote add origin https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git
  $ so --human remote list

Learn more:
  A command's help  so remote <command> --help
  Guide             https://swarmops.cc/docs/guides/github-remote
  Reference         https://swarmops.cc/docs/reference/cli

Options:
      --repo <STORE>     The store to use (default: $SWARMOPS_REPO)
      --as <AGENT>       The agent to act as, <family>/<instance> (default:
                         $SWARMOPS_AGENT)
      --json             Print the JSON envelope: the default, unless
                         $SWARMOPS_FORMAT is human
      --human            Print a short text rendering instead of JSON
      --pretty[=<BOOL>]  Pretty-print the JSON (default: when stdout is a
                         terminal)
  -h, --help             Print help

$ so auth --help
Keep, list or remove your logins, or hand one to git: a token per host, in one
file of your own

Usage: so auth [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  login           Log in to a provider, and keep its token
  status          List your logins, without their tokens
  logout          Remove a provider's login
  git-credential  Answer git's credential-helper protocol

Examples:
  $ so auth login --gh --with-token < token.txt
  $ so --human auth status

Learn more:
  A command's help  so auth <command> --help
  Guide             https://swarmops.cc/docs/guides/github-remote
  Reference         https://swarmops.cc/docs/reference/cli

Options:
      --repo <STORE>     The store to use (default: $SWARMOPS_REPO)
      --as <AGENT>       The agent to act as, <family>/<instance> (default:
                         $SWARMOPS_AGENT)
      --json             Print the JSON envelope: the default, unless
                         $SWARMOPS_FORMAT is human
